msgid "磁盘管理器（Diskmgr）"
msgstr "Disk Manager (Diskmgr)"

msgid ""
"运行 ``diskmgr``，或从系统菜单打开磁盘管理器。程序使用 C++、FLTK 和 X11， 沿用系统 FLTK "
"主题、中文字体及现有磁盘管理器图标。左侧选择磁盘，右侧选择 分区；工具栏与“分区”菜单提供同一组操作。Ctrl+R 刷新，Ctrl+Q 关闭。"
msgstr ""
"Run ``diskmgr`` or open Disk Manager from the system menu. The program uses "
"C++, FLTK, and X11, retaining the system FLTK theme, Chinese fonts, and "
"existing disk manager icon. Select a disk on the left and a partition on the"
" right. The toolbar and Partition menu offer the same operations. Ctrl+R "
"refreshes; Ctrl+Q closes."

msgid ""
"支持查看 GPT 分区、文件系统、容量、PARTUUID 和实际挂载位置；在空闲空间 "
"新建并格式化分区，格式化、删除分区，以及挂载和卸载数据分区。新文件系统 可选 ext4、FAT32、exFAT，也可挂载现有 ext2 "
"分区。现有格式化器要求 FAT32 至少32 MiB，ext4/exFAT至少128 MiB；较小分区不能使用对应格式化器。分区名称支持中文，磁盘上 "
"使用 GPT 规定的 UTF-16，界面使用 UTF-8；超过36个 UTF-16编码单元的名称被拒绝。 "
"界面输入另有71字节上限，分区表显示超出列宽时可调整列宽或水平滚动。"
msgstr ""
"You can inspect GPT partitions, filesystems, capacities, PARTUUIDs, and "
"actual mount locations; create and format partitions in free space; format "
"or delete partitions; and mount or unmount data partitions. New filesystems "
"can be ext4, FAT32, or exFAT; existing ext2 partitions can also be mounted. "
"Current formatters require at least 32 MiB for FAT32 and 128 MiB for "
"ext4/exFAT; smaller partitions cannot use the corresponding formatter. "
"Partition names support Chinese, using GPT-mandated UTF-16 on disk and UTF-8"
" in the interface. Names longer than 36 UTF-16 code units are rejected, and "
"interface input has a separate 71-byte limit. Resize columns or scroll "
"horizontally if partition-table content exceeds the column width."

msgid ""
"普通用户默认只读；“以管理员身份打开…”使用标准 sudo 验证当前用户密码， 成功后打开 root 窗口。需要该用户已有 sudo "
"权限；密码通过标准输入传送， 不进入命令行或环境变量。取消或验证失败保留原窗口。"
msgstr ""
"Regular users default to read-only access. Open as Administrator… uses "
"standard sudo to verify the current user's password, then opens a root "
"window on success. The user must already have sudo authorization. The "
"password is sent through standard input, never command lines or environment "
"variables. Cancellation or authentication failure preserves the original "
"window."

msgid ""
"新建、格式化和删除需要输入对话框给出的 CREATE、FORMAT、DELETE，连续点击 "
"两次确认。修改任意字段会取消第一次确认。系统分区和已挂载分区受到保护； 含挂载分区的整盘不能更改 GPT。BIOS Boot 分区不能格式化或挂载。 "
"扫描和磁盘操作在独立子进程执行，期间窗口继续处理 X11 事件，操作完成后 刷新列表；操作进行中不能关闭窗口。新建成功但格式化失败会明确报告部分成功。"
msgstr ""
"Create, Format, and Delete require typing CREATE, FORMAT, or DELETE as "
"specified in the dialog and clicking confirmation twice consecutively. "
"Changing any field cancels the first confirmation. System and mounted "
"partitions are protected; GPT cannot be changed on a disk containing mounted"
" partitions. BIOS Boot partitions cannot be formatted or mounted. Scans and "
"disk operations run in separate child processes while the window continues "
"handling X11 events, with lists refreshed afterward. The window cannot be "
"closed during an operation. Successful creation followed by failed "
"formatting is explicitly reported as partial success."

msgid ""
"使用现有 POSIX 文件操作、Linux 块设备 ioctl 和 mount/umount2，支持512字节 逻辑扇区和有效 GPT。没有 GPT "
"或分区表损坏的磁盘 仅报告错误，需先用独立工具准备 GPT。挂载点为 ``/mnt/disk<编号>p<分区号>``， "
"已有挂载、符号链接、权限不安全或非空目录会被拒绝。"
msgstr ""
"The program uses existing POSIX file operations, Linux block-device ioctls, "
"and mount/umount2, supporting 512-byte logical sectors and valid GPT. Disks "
"without GPT or with damaged partition tables only produce errors; prepare "
"GPT with a separate tool first. Mount points use ``/mnt/disk<编号>p<分区号>``. "
"Existing mounts, symbolic links, unsafe permissions, and nonempty "
"directories are rejected."

msgid ""
"写入前重新检查设备节点、GPT 头、分区 GUID、范围、只读、diskseq 及挂载状态。 "
"设备热插拔后应刷新并重新选择目标。已打开对象保留原介质身份。普通文件描述符读写按文件权限验证， 重读分区表需要 Linux "
"``CAP_SYS_ADMIN``，与上游 `Linux 块设备 ioctl 实现 "
"<https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/block/ioctl.c>`_ 一致。"
msgstr ""
"Before writing, device nodes, GPT headers, partition GUIDs, ranges, read-"
"only state, diskseq, and mounts are rechecked. Refresh and reselect the "
"target after device hotplug. Open objects retain the original medium's "
"identity. Ordinary descriptor reads/writes are checked against file "
"permissions; rereading the partition table requires Linux ``CAP_SYS_ADMIN``,"
" consistent with upstream's `Linux block-device ioctl implementation "
"<https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/block/ioctl.c>`_."
